        "read": false,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "What is the consensus on when the game actually ends upon the destruction of the villain? For example, will hit-backs like Backlash Field or the Chairman&#39;s ability activate when the villain is reduced to 0 or fewer HP (assuming all other conditions for victory have been fulfilled)?\n\nAccording to the Handelabra/Christopher fireside chat,\n\n[quote=\"MigrantP\"]\n\nIf the Wraith has Combat Stance in play and is incapacitated by damage, Combat Stance is removed from play before its effect can occur.\n\n[/quote]\n\nHowever, in my experiments with the digital version of Sentinels, this rule doesn&#39;t apply to villains: both Ambuscade (with Reactive Plating) and Baron Blade (with Backlash Field) still get to strike back after being reduced to 0 or fewer HP. This makes it possible for<em> all</em> the characters, villain and hero, to be incapacitated/destroyed (which results in a villain victory, apparently).\n\nAt what point do you check for victory? And why do only villains seem to get a pass on striking back from the grave?\n",
